@page "/display/alert"
@using Swallow.Components.Display

<PageHeader Title="Alert" />
<SupportedRenderModes Static WebSocket WebAssembly />

<p>
    A message box for fixed content. This is not meant to be used as a reaction
    to indicate success or failure of an operation (i.e. a toast), but rather
    for a (mostly) constant message to the user. A hint that something needs
    to be taken care of, for example.
</p>

<SectionHeader Title="Examples" Anchor="example" />

<p>
    Plain alerts can be rendered with just a message.
</p>

<ComponentExample>
    <SwAlert>You didn't bring out the trash yet!</SwAlert>
</ComponentExample>

<p>You can also set a title for the alert.</p>

<ComponentExample>
    <SwAlert>
        <Title>Warning</Title>
        <Content>You haven't set a destination yet.</Content>
    </SwAlert>
</ComponentExample>

<p>
    Additional styling, e.g. applying colors using <code class="sw">sw-red</code>, is possible.
</p>

<ComponentExample>
    <SwAlert class="sw-red">Device is not connected.</SwAlert>
</ComponentExample>

<SectionHeader Title="Reference" Anchor="reference" />

<p>
    <code class="sw">@nameof(SwAlert)</code>: <InlineDocumentation Type="@typeof(SwAlert)" />
</p>

<ComponentParameterTable TComponent="SwAlert" />
